      </figure>

      <section>
        <h2>Background</h2>
        <p>Video games have developed from simple single-player experiences
           into large online communities. Games such as Counter-Strike,
           League of Legends, and Valorant have helped competitive gaming
           become popular around the world.</p>
        <p>The growth of <abbr title="Electronic Sports">eSports</abbr> has
           also created professional teams, tournaments, and streaming
           careers. Faster internet connections and better gaming hardware
           have made online competition more accessible.</p>
      </section>

      <blockquote cite="https://www.w3.org">
        <p>Games bring people together through competition, creativity,
           and shared experiences.</p>
        <footer>— <cite>Gaming Community Research</cite></footer>
      </blockquote>

      <section>
        <h2>Analysis</h2>
        <p>Modern competitive games require players to improve their
           reaction time, communication, and strategy. Players also adjust
           settings such as <code>graphics</code>, sensitivity, and frame
           rate to improve their performance.</p>
        <p>With the growth of streaming platforms and professional
           tournaments, <mark>gaming has become a major form of entertainment</mark>
           for millions of people around the world.</p>
      </section>

